        "original_id": "55a98e3b-a6c7-526f-8c15-c371f92cabec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Lane, Lucille Ball, Jim Brochu, Steve Schalchlin, John Bettis, Marie Cain\n- Products: I Love Lucy, The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour, The Lucy Show, Here's Lucy, Life with Lucy, Lucy in the Afternoon, MythBusters, The Last Session\n- Roles: supporting actor, authority figure, comedic foe, author\n\nFacts:\n- Lucille Ball was best known as the star of the self-produced sitcoms \"I Love Lucy,\" \"The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour,\" \"The Lucy Show,\" \"Here's Lucy,\" and \"Life with Lucy.\"\n- Charles Lane was a favored supporting actor of Lucille Ball, who often cast him as a no-nonsense authority figure and comedic foe opposite her scatterbrained TV character on \"I Love Lucy,\" \"The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour,\" and \"The Lucy Show.\"\n- Jim Brochu was a friend of Lucille Ball and the author of the unauthorized biography \"Lucy in the Afternoon.\"\n- Jim Brochu appeared on an episode of \"MythBusters\" in his capacity as the author of \"Lucy in the Afternoon.\"\n- \"The Last Session\" is a musical with a book by Jim Brochu, music and lyrics by Steve Schalchlin, and additional lyrics by John Bettis and Marie Cain.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
